      "explanation": "In French, dates are expressed using the structure: le + cardinal number + month + year. For example, le 5 janvier (January 5th), le 15 juillet (July 15th). The only exception is the first day of the month: use 'le premier' instead of 'le un'. For example, le premier mars (March 1st). Note that months are never capitalized in French and do not change form.",
